{"units": [{"id": "ekphthino-quote2", "translation": "A countless host of men has perished."}, {"id": "ekphobeo-orth1", "translation": "to frighten out"}, {"id": "ekphobeo-def1", "translation": "to frighten out"}, {"id": "ekphobeo-quote1", "translation": "Such a shock of evils frightens the mind."}, {"id": "ekphora-orth1", "translation": "carrying out (of a corpse), funeral procession"}, {"id": "ekphora-def1", "translation": "carrying out"}, {"id": "ekphora-note1", "translation": "Concerning a funeral"}, {"id": "ekphora-quote1", "translation": "And to be without honor in the carrying out by friends."}, {"id": "ekphora-quote2", "translation": "In hostile funeral processions."}, {"id": "ekphora-quote3", "translation": "At the carrying out of a corpse."}, {"id": "ekphoros-orth1", "translation": "carrying out"}, {"id": "ekphoros-def1", "translation": "carrying out"}, {"id": "ekphoros-note1", "translation": "Schuetz expressed the sense correctly, but if there are impious men, I do not hinder you from rooting them out."}, {"id": "ekphoros-quote1", "translation": "May you be more carrying out of the impious."}, {"id": "ekphrazo-orth1", "translation": "to tell out, declare"}, {"id": "ekphrazo-def1", "translation": "to tell out, declare"}, {"id": "ekphrazo-quote1", "translation": "Tell each thing again."}, {"id": "ekphyngano-orth1", "translation": "to flee out, escape"}, {"id": "ekphyngano-def1", "translation": "to flee out, escape"}, {"id": "ekphyngano-quote1", "translation": "I escape unseemly bonds and miseries."}, {"id": "ekphysao-orth1", "translation": "to blow out, pour forth"}, {"id": "ekphysao-def1", "translation": "to blow out, pour forth"}, {"id": "ekphysao-quote1", "translation": "Where a river pours forth its might."}, {"id": "ekphysiao-orth1", "translation": "to blow out, exhale"}, {"id": "ekphysiao-def1", "translation": "to blow out, exhale"}, {"id": "ekphysiao-quote1", "translation": "Blowing out a sharp slaughter of blood."}, {"id": "ekphysis-orth1", "translation": "a growing out, eruption"}, {"id": "ekphysis-def1", "translation": "that which grows out or bursts forth"}, {"id": "ekphysis-quote1", "translation": "He fixed a terrible, mouth-like eruption."}, {"id": "ekcheo-orth1", "translation": "to pour out"}, {"id": "ekcheo-def1", "translation": "to pour out"}, {"id": "ekcheo-note1", "translation": "where ἐκχέασα [having poured out] is more probable."}, {"id": "ekcheo-note2", "translation": "ἐκχέας [having poured out] corrupted from ἐγχέας [having poured in]."}, {"id": "ekcheo-note3", "translation": "Improperly"}, {"id": "ekcheo-quote1", "translation": "Having poured out the kindred blood of my mother on the ground."}, {"id": "ekcheo-quote2", "translation": "Pouring out this earth-drunk libation,"}, {"id": "ekcheo-quote3", "translation": "For someone having poured out everything in exchange for one blood."}, {"id": "ekcheo-quote4", "translation": "Let no one pour out great wealth."}, {"id": "ekcheo-quote5", "translation": "The heart, anticipating the tongue, would pour out these things."}, {"id": "ekcheo-word1", "translation": "having poured out (feminine)"}, {"id": "ekcheo-word2", "translation": "having poured out (masculine)"}, {"id": "ekcheo-word3", "translation": "having poured in"}, {"id": "ekon-orth1", "translation": "willing, voluntarily"}, {"id": "ekon-def1", "translation": "willing, doing something voluntarily or gladly"}, {"id": "ekon-note1", "translation": "Thus Wieseler for ἐκ τῶνδ᾽ [from these things]."}, {"id": "ekon-quote1", "translation": "Willing to stand as an ally with willing Zeus."}, {"id": "ekon-quote2", "translation": "Willingly, willingly I erred."}, {"id": "ekon-quote3", "translation": "She will not come willingly."}, {"id": "ekon-quote4", "translation": "Willingly I speak to those who understand."}, {"id": "ekon-quote5", "translation": "Who sailed not willingly,"}, {"id": "ekon-quote6", "translation": "But yield the power to me willingly."}, {"id": "ekon-quote7", "translation": "For no one willingly uses the yoke of slavery."}, {"id": "ekon-quote8", "translation": "But you say that this man killed willingly."}, {"id": "ekon-quote9", "translation": "If I betray them willingly."}, {"id": "ekon-quote10", "translation": "Willingly, without compulsion."}, {"id": "ekon-quote11", "translation": "And these women willingly—you may lead them."}, {"id": "ekon-word1", "translation": "from these things"}, {"id": "elaia-orth1", "translation": "olive tree"}, {"id": "elaia-def1", "translation": "olive tree"}, {"id": "elaia-note1", "translation": "On the Attic form ἐλάα [olive] and on the distinction between ἐλαία [olive] and ἐλάα [olive] invented by certain grammarians, see Thes. vol. 3 p. 655."}, {"id": "elaia-quote1", "translation": "The fragrant fruit of the yellow olive."}, {"id": "elaia-quote2", "translation": "Shaded by the branches of the olive."}, {"id": "elaia-quote3", "translation": "And the high-born branch of the olive."}, {"id": "elaia-word1", "translation": "olive"}, {"id": "elaia-word2", "translation": "olive"}, {"id": "elaia-word3", "translation": "olive"}, {"id": "elaiophytos-orth1", "translation": "planted with olives"}, {"id": "elaiophytos-def1", "translation": "planted with olives"}, {"id": "elaiophytos-quote1", "translation": "And Samos planted with olives."}, {"id": "helandros-orth1", "translation": "destroying men"}, {"id": "helandros-def1", "translation": "destroying men"}, {"id": "helandros-note1", "translation": "concerning Helen"}, {"id": "helandros-quote1", "translation": "Ship-destroying, man-destroying, city-destroying."}, {"id": "elasson-orth1", "translation": "smaller, less"}, {"id": "elasson-def1", "translation": "smaller, less"}, {"id": "elasson-note1", "translation": "Bothius wanted the words καὶ τὸν ἐλάσσονα [and the smaller] to be deleted."}, {"id": "elasson-quote1", "translation": "The great one quickly swallows the half-opon and the smaller (ἐλάσσω [smaller] Porson)."}, {"id": "elasson-quote2", "translation": "But to me there is less care for Zeus than nothing."}, {"id": "elasson-quote3", "translation": "They suffer no less."}, {"id": "elasson-word1", "translation": "and the smaller"}, {"id": "elater-orth1", "translation": "driver, charioteer"}, {"id": "elater-def1", "translation": "driver, charioteer"}, {"id": "elater-note1", "translation": "Concerning a horseman"}, {"id": "elater-quote1", "translation": "And Sosthanes, driver of horses."}, {"id": "elaterios-orth1", "translation": "able to drive away, averting"}, {"id": "elaterios-def1", "translation": "having the power of driving away or averting"}, {"id": "elaterios-quote1", "translation": "With purifications that drive away ruin."}, {"id": "elauno-orth1", "translation": "to drive, push, thrust"}, {"id": "elauno-def1", "translation": "[with imperfect ἤλauvov, aorist ἤλασα, future ἐλῶ contracted from ἐλάσω, passive ἐλαύνομαι, and perfect participle ἐληλαμέναι, and aorist ἠλάθην] to drive, push, thrust."}, {"id": "elauno-def2", "translation": "to subdue"}, {"id": "elauno-def3", "translation": "Concerning building a wall"}, {"id": "elauno-note1", "translation": "Concerning expelling a pollution"}, {"id": "elauno-note2", "translation": "where Weilius reads ἐλαθῇ [may be driven]."}, {"id": "elauno-note3", "translation": "in several copies"}, {"id": "elauno-note4", "translation": "where in M is Ἑλλάνων [of the Greeks]."}]}